# Test environment. Committed on purpose: it holds dummy values plus a local,
# disposable database, so a clean checkout can run the suite with no hosted
# services. Nothing here is a real secret, and no hosted database may be added.
#
# The database is a throwaway Postgres container. Start it before running the
# end to end suite:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml up -d --wait
# and remove it afterwards with:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml down -v
#
# The end to end run drops every row and reseeds, so this must never point at a
# database you care about. Port 5433 keeps it clear of a Postgres you may
# already be running on the default 5432.
#
# Nothing loads this file on its own. It is read three ways:
#   - prisma.config.ts when NODE_ENV=test (Prisma CLI commands)
#   - `node --env-file=.env.test prisma/seed.js` (the end to end reset)
#   - playwright.config.mjs, which hands the values to the server it boots
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/intelligrade_test?schema=public"
# schema.prisma declares directUrl for Supabase's connection pooler. There is no
# pooler in front of the test container, so the direct connection is the same
# URL. The variable still has to be set, or Prisma fails with P1012.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/intelligrade_test?schema=public"
GEMINI_API_KEY="test-gemini-key-not-real"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://test.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="test-supabase-service-role-key-not-real"
